WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.160
- [Instructor] We're told
that Cara had a tower

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.650
with 42 blocks.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.380
She added 12 red blocks,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.360
14 more blue blocks,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.140
and 16 purple blocks.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.530
So what we want to do in this video

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.650
is think about how many
total blocks Cara now has.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.380
And to help us with that,

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.480
we are going to set up a little
bit of a number line here.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.800
And this number line, it keeps
going in both directions,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.100
and I'm going to set it up so

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.860
this big, thick hash mark here is 40.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.450
I wanna make sure that
I can include 42 here.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.174
And you can see, we go 41, 42, 43, 44, 45,

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.690
46, 47, 48, 49, 50.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.600
So each of the thick ones are 10 more.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.600
So that's 50, 60, 70, and 80.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.270
What I'd like you to
do is pause this video,

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.300
think about where 42
is on this number line,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.570
and then think about how
do we add these blocks

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:01.980
on this number line to think about

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.653
how many total blocks Cara now has.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.940
All right, now let's do this together.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.810
So let's start with her starting point,

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.140
the 42 blocks right over here.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.730
So we see this is 40.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.450
So we go 41, 42.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.980
So this right over here
is Cara's starting point.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.700
That is 42 blocks.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.450
Now first she adds 12 red blocks.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.470
So you could just count
on the number line.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.940
So if you add one, two,
three, four, five, six,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:37.480
seven, eight, nine, 10, 11, 12,

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.200
you get right over there.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.200
So this right over here is
all of us adding 12 blocks.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.860
Now where does that get us to?

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.500
Well we can see that we are now

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.410
one, two, three, four past 50.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.363
So we are now at 54.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.750
Right over there.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.910
And you could have done it another way.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:59.530
You could have just added
right from the get-go.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.517
You could have said, "All
right, I'm going to add 12,

00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:04.957
"so it takes me eight to get to 50

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:08.880
"and then I have four
more left, gets me to 54."

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.940
And then we need to add
those 14 more blue blocks.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.700
So let's add 14 from here.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.700
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight,

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.130
nine, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14,

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:25.690
gets us right over there.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.900
So we add another 14, we get over there.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.550
And now what number are we at?

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.070
Well, there's two ways to think about it.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.330
You can see that we are
one, two, three, four,

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.270
five, six, seven, eight above 60,

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:41.930
which would tell us we're at 68,

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.070
or you could see that we are two below 70,

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.780
which would also be 68.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.280
So we're now at 68 total blocks.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.130
And then we add the 16 purple blocks.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:52.050
So let's do that.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:57.010
Let's add one, two, three,
four, five, six, seven, eight,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.900
nine, 10, 11, 12, 13,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.000
14, 15, 16

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.250
and we get right over there.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.790
We're very lucky that our number line

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.490
just happened to have
the right number of marks

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:10.530
right over here.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:15.380
So then we add 16 and
we can see that we are

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.490
one, two, three, four past 80.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.140
So we're at 84 total blocks.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.950
Another way you could
have thought about it is

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.750
it would have taken us
two blocks to go to 70,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.640
then we would have 14 left.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.850
Another 10 to get to 80 and
then we would have four left

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.790
and then you get to 84.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.343
But now Cara has a total of 84 blocks.

